$DIR/main.p:17:5: second is a second //pu:scheduler variable; the first is first at $DIR/main.p:12:5: a program binds one scheduler (language spec section 4.7)
    A program binds its scheduler with one package-level variable marked
    //pu:scheduler, whose type, not an interface, implements rt.Scheduler:
    NewTask, FreeTask, Spawn, Park, Wake and Yield. The runtime calls its
    methods directly. This variable does not qualify, or the program marks more
    than one.
    The scheduler is chosen when the program is linked, like the panic handler,
    so the runtime calls it without an indirection and a program cannot run
    without one.
    (see "go starts a puroutine" in the Plutonium spec, section 4.7)
    (run "pluto explain E2582" for a longer explanation)

$DIR/main.p:12:5: //pu:scheduler variable first of type main.half does not implement rt.Scheduler (missing method FreeTask)
    (explained above; run "pluto explain E2582" for more)
